WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.910
A uranium-238 nucleus is unstable,
but nothing triggers its decay:

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.250
heat, pressure and
chemistry don't change it.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.560
Then, without warning, it
emits an alpha particle,

4
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.490
and it is no longer uranium.

5
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.040
It is thorium.

6
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.710
Some nuclei go on decaying in a
chain, one step after another.

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.960
Could three decays in a row bring a
nucleus back to the very element it started

8
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.010
as?

9
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.650
In this mission, you'll meet the
radiations a nucleus can emit,

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.810
and what each one is made of.

11
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.280
Then you'll balance decay equations,
keeping track of every nucleon and every

12
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.380
charge.

13
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.770
Your mission: predict whether a nucleus
can return to its starting element after

14
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.000
three decays.
